WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.500 --> 00:00:02.130
- [Instructor] So what we're
going to do in this video

00:00:02.130 --> 00:00:03.917
is build our muscles at comparing numbers

00:00:03.917 --> 00:00:07.810
that are represented in different ways.

00:00:07.810 --> 00:00:12.305
So, for example, over here
on the left we have 0.37,

00:00:12.305 --> 00:00:15.480
you could also view this
as thirty-seven hundredths,

00:00:15.480 --> 00:00:19.540
and on the right we have 307 thousandths.

00:00:19.540 --> 00:00:21.840
And so, what I want you
to do is pause this video,

00:00:21.840 --> 00:00:24.830
and figure out, are these
equal to each other?

00:00:24.830 --> 00:00:26.630
Or is one of the larger than the other?

00:00:26.630 --> 00:00:28.780
And if one of them is,
which one is larger,

00:00:29.663 --> 00:00:30.496
and which one is smaller?

00:00:30.496 --> 00:00:31.621
Pause this video and
try to figure that out.

00:00:31.621 --> 00:00:32.710
All right,

00:00:32.710 --> 00:00:33.980
now let's try to do this together,

00:00:33.980 --> 00:00:35.470
and the way that my brain works is,

00:00:35.470 --> 00:00:39.141
I try to put them into
a common representation.

00:00:39.141 --> 00:00:41.110
So, one way we could do it is

00:00:41.110 --> 00:00:45.760
we could try to re-write this
one on the right as a decimal.

00:00:45.760 --> 00:00:47.420
So let's do that.

00:00:47.420 --> 00:00:50.920
So, we could re-write this as,

00:00:50.920 --> 00:00:54.300
it's expressing a certain
number of thousandths,

00:00:54.300 --> 00:00:57.878
so let me just make some
blanks for our various placeS.

00:00:57.878 --> 00:00:58.711
So let's say that's the one's place,

00:00:58.711 --> 00:00:59.750
and that's our decimal,

00:00:59.750 --> 00:01:02.090
that's going to be our tenth's place,

00:01:02.090 --> 00:01:04.150
that's going to be our hundredth's place,

00:01:04.150 --> 00:01:07.380
and that's going to be
our thousandth's place.

00:01:07.380 --> 00:01:10.410
So, one way to view 307 thousandths

00:01:10.410 --> 00:01:15.410
is that we have 307 of this
place, right over there.

00:01:15.580 --> 00:01:18.030
So, we could just write the seven there,

00:01:18.030 --> 00:01:18.863
the zero there,

00:01:18.863 --> 00:01:19.696
and the three over there.

00:01:19.696 --> 00:01:22.980
This over here would be 307 thousandths,

00:01:22.980 --> 00:01:25.140
and so we would have no ones.

00:01:25.140 --> 00:01:26.847
And so when you look at it this way,

00:01:26.847 --> 00:01:29.790
it's a little bit easier to compare.

00:01:29.790 --> 00:01:31.049
You can say, "all right,

00:01:31.049 --> 00:01:33.646
we have the same number of ones,

00:01:33.646 --> 00:01:36.080
we have the same number of tenths,

00:01:36.080 --> 00:01:37.940
let me compare the like
one to the like ones."

00:01:37.940 --> 00:01:40.180
So, our tenths are equal,

00:01:40.180 --> 00:01:43.350
but what happens when we
get to the hundredths?

00:01:43.350 --> 00:01:45.850
Here, we have seven hundredths,

00:01:45.850 --> 00:01:48.705
and here we have zero hundredths.

00:01:48.705 --> 00:01:53.190
So, this number on the
left is going to be larger.

00:01:53.190 --> 00:01:58.190
So, 37 hundredths is greater
than 307 thousandths.

00:01:59.800 --> 00:02:01.530
Another that we could have done this

00:02:01.530 --> 00:02:04.180
is we could have
re-expressed this left number

00:02:04.180 --> 00:02:05.890
in terms of thousandths.

00:02:05.890 --> 00:02:09.200
We could've re-written it
as, instead of 37 hundredths,

00:02:09.200 --> 00:02:11.880
we could've just said
zero point three seven,

00:02:11.880 --> 00:02:13.600
and just put another zero on the right,

00:02:13.600 --> 00:02:17.400
and this is 370 thousandths.

00:02:17.400 --> 00:02:18.240
I'll write it out.

00:02:18.240 --> 00:02:22.290
370 thousandths.

00:02:22.290 --> 00:02:23.870
And when you look at it this way,

00:02:23.870 --> 00:02:26.520
once again it's clear
that 370 of something

00:02:26.520 --> 00:02:29.580
is more than 307 of that something.

00:02:29.580 --> 00:02:32.640
So, this quantity on the left is larger.

00:02:32.640 --> 00:02:33.770
Let's do another example,

00:02:33.770 --> 00:02:35.776
but I'll use different formats.

00:02:35.776 --> 00:02:40.130
So, let's say on the left,

00:02:40.130 --> 00:02:41.690
I'll use decimal format,

00:02:41.690 --> 00:02:44.646
I'll have zero point six, or six tenths,

00:02:44.646 --> 00:02:46.150
and then on the right,

00:02:46.150 --> 00:02:51.150
I'm going to have six
times one over a hundred.

00:02:51.290 --> 00:02:52.942
Pause this video and tell me,

00:02:52.942 --> 00:02:55.900
which of these quantities,
if either, are greater,

00:02:55.900 --> 00:02:57.573
or are they equal to each other?

00:02:59.130 --> 00:03:01.410
All right, so once again,
in order to tackle this,

00:03:01.410 --> 00:03:02.780
you really just have to think about

00:03:02.780 --> 00:03:04.570
what are different way to represent them?

00:03:04.570 --> 00:03:07.026
And really just get to
a common representation.

00:03:07.026 --> 00:03:12.026
And so, I could re-write six
tenths and six times one tenth.

00:03:13.150 --> 00:03:15.280
Six times one tenth.

00:03:15.280 --> 00:03:18.149
And this might be enough to
be able to compare the two,

00:03:18.149 --> 00:03:21.540
because six times one tenth,

00:03:21.540 --> 00:03:23.680
is that going to be
greater than, or less than,

00:03:23.680 --> 00:03:25.806
or equal to six times a hundredth?

00:03:25.806 --> 00:03:30.324
Well, a tenth is ten times
larger than a hundredth,

00:03:30.324 --> 00:03:33.840
so because this is ten
times larger than that,

00:03:33.840 --> 00:03:36.010
if you multiply is by six, well,

00:03:36.010 --> 00:03:37.620
this is going to be a larger quantity.

00:03:37.620 --> 00:03:41.147
So we could go and say, "Hey,
this is greater than that."

00:03:41.147 --> 00:03:43.970
Another way that you
might have realized that

00:03:43.970 --> 00:03:46.452
is if you were to express
this right quantity

00:03:46.452 --> 00:03:48.970
as a decimal like this.

00:03:48.970 --> 00:03:53.140
So, this is six times a
hundredth, or six hundredths.

00:03:53.140 --> 00:03:54.867
So, we could write that's our ones,

00:03:54.867 --> 00:03:56.460
that's our tenths,

00:03:56.460 --> 00:04:00.030
and then in our hundredths
place, you would have six.

00:04:00.030 --> 00:04:02.970
And if it isn't obvious
that this is less than that,

00:04:02.970 --> 00:04:04.843
you could add a zero here,

00:04:04.843 --> 00:04:08.165
and this, we would read as 60 hundredths,

00:04:08.165 --> 00:04:13.165
and 60 hundredths is for sure
larger than six hundredths.

00:04:14.150 --> 00:04:16.544
So, these are all very reasonable ways

00:04:16.544 --> 00:04:19.050
of re-representing these
numbers and putting them

00:04:19.050 --> 00:04:21.110
in the same format so we
can make the comparison

00:04:21.110 --> 00:04:23.910
and realize the one on the left,
actually in both scenarios,

00:04:23.910 --> 00:04:25.710
is larger than the one on the right.

